-- title:
--   Descended chart and supersingular valuation ring as G-invariants
-- statement:
--   The data are: a prime $q$; a nonzero natural number $M'$; a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, with residue field $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$; a finite set $W$ of places of the modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M' = \kappa(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{M'}))$ over $\kappa$ (a place being a valuation subring containing the constants, proper, with principal ideals); a hypothesis `hle` that $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $\mathbb Q$-field generated by the $\mathsf q$-expansions $j(\mathsf q^d)$, $d \mid M'$, is contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with residue field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, and the compatibilities of the structure `ConstantReduction` (membership of constants, reduction of constants, existence of scalings with nonzero residue, preservation of degrees, push-forward of divisors); and a distinguished element $s \in W$.
--
--   There are further data entering only as the arguments of the hypothesis record $\mathcal F$ below: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$ (hypothesis `hπ`), a natural number $\ell$, elements $\zeta_0, \varpi_t \in k_0$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ which is the pullback of $A$ (hypothesis `hAb`) and an element $\varpi_b \in A_b$, a prime $\ell'$, an element $\xi \in k_0$, an intermediate field $K_{\ell}$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ carrying an algebra structure over $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) compatible with $k_0$, a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$, an ideal $y$ of the $j$-finite chart $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K_\ell\,j_\ell$ (the elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$), a subalgebra $\tilde B$ of $K_\ell$ over $A_0$ and a valuation subring $\tilde W$ of $K_\ell$ with $\tilde B \subseteq \tilde W$ (hypothesis `hBW`), a natural number $n$, an element $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, an automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$, a natural number $m$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, a proof `hjK` that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell') = j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$ lies in $K_\ell$, an element $a_0 \in A_0$, and a finite set `ends` of subrings of $K_\ell$. All standing assumptions on these data are bundled in $\mathcal F$, a term of the structure [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.RigidDescentHyps`](def/ModularCurve_RigidDescentHyps.html#L28) applied to exactly the above arguments; the statement imposes no further conditions on them.
--
--   Finally, the descent data. A subgroup $G$ of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ is assumed (hypothesis `hG`) to be the subgroup generated by those $\tau$ for which there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$; this predicate says that for every weight $k$, every pair of modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with integral $\mathsf q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and $p_g$ having nonzero image over $\mathbb Q$, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau x$ times the $\mathsf q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $\mathsf q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell')\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ attached to $\gamma = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d\end{pmatrix}$. Further, $K_0$ is the fixed field of $G$ in $K_\ell$ (hypothesis `hK₀`), $B_0$ is the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the elements of $\tilde B$ fixed by every element of $G$ (hypothesis `hB₀`), and $W_0'$ is a valuation subring of $K_0$ whose elements are exactly those whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $\tilde W$ (hypothesis `hW₀'`).
--
--   The conclusion is the conjunction of the following.
--
--   First, for every $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$.
--
--   Second, $W_0'$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Third, the image of $\pi_0$ in $K_0$ lies in $W_0'$ and the maximal ideal of $W_0'$ is generated by it.
--
--   Fourth, a specialisation clause over the place $s$: for every $g$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, assuming (i) that for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j(\mathsf q))$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$, and (ii) that the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, then for any proof that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K_\ell$, this element lies in $K_0$, its class lies in $W_0'$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ such that the residue of $c$ in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of the class of $g(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0'$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0'$.
--
--   Fifth, stability of $W_0'$ under the level automorphisms: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every automorphism $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ over $k_0$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, and every $f \in K_\ell$ with both $f \in K_0$ and $\tau f \in K_0$: the class of $f$ lies in $W_0'$ if and only if the class of $\tau f$ does.
--
--   Sixth, a conjunction of assertions about $B_0$: the structure map $A_0 \to B_0$ agrees in $K_\ell$ with the inclusion of $k_0$; $B_0 \subseteq K_0$; every $f \in K_0$ can be written as $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_0$ and $h \neq 0$; $B_0$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_0$; the quotient of $B_0$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every $f \in B_0$ lies in $K_0$ and its class lies in $W_0'$; the image of $\pi_0$ in $B_0$ is a prime element; an element $f \in K_0$ lies in $W_0'$ if and only if $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in B_0$ and the image of $\pi_0$ not dividing $h$ (so $W_0'$ is the localisation of $B_0$ at $(\pi_0)$); for any proof that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ of the coefficientwise image of $j(\mathsf q)$ lies in $K_\ell$, that element lies in $B_0$; and $B_0$ is stable under every $\tau$ attached as above to some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   The last conjunct of this sixth group is a reduction statement in characteristic $q$: for every algebra structure of $\mathbb F_{q^2} = \mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ on $\kappa$ and every hypothesis that the Drinfeld coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa = \kappa[x_0,x_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ is a domain, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_0$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$, the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta)$ with $\zeta \in C_s$, such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ equals $2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, that is, twice $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(j)$ divided by the $j$-ramification of $s$; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_0 \to B_0$ is the reduction map $A_0 \to \kappa$ followed by $\kappa \to \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$; every $z$ in $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g, h \in B_0$ and $\rho(h) \neq 0$; an element $z$ of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ lies in the image of $\rho$ if and only if, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, it lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and $\rho$ is equivariant for the level automorphisms, in the sense that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $\tau$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, every proof that the pair $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ (the kernel of the character $(\delta,u) \mapsto \det(\delta)\,u^{q+1}$), and every $f \in B_0$ with $\tau f \in B_0$, the image $\rho(\tau f)$ in the Drinfeld function field equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$.
--
--   This is the upstairs half of the level-descent step in the construction of the model of a modular curve at a supersingular point: the $G$-invariants of the rigid chart $(\tilde B, \tilde W)$ are identified as a smooth affine chart $B_0$ with fraction field $K_0$, a discrete valuation ring $W_0' = (B_0)_{(\pi_0)}$ lying over the supersingular place $s$ and stable under the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level automorphisms, whose special fibre is described by a ring homomorphism onto an $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-rational quotient of the Drinfeld curve function field, equivariantly for the level action. It is used in the assembly of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart); no assertion about nodes is made here.
